WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.932
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:08.468
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.768 --> 00:00:15.158
Unit fifteen: Traditions and Festivals. In this unit, you will describe Cambodian traditions and ceremonies.

4
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.058
offering.

5
00:00:17.758 --> 00:00:22.196
offering means food, flowers or money given at a temple or to spirits.

6
00:00:22.496 --> 00:00:24.867
Families bring offerings of fruit to the pagoda.

7
00:00:25.567 --> 00:00:28.010
Your turn. Say: offering.

8
00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:31.723
offering.

9
00:00:32.717 --> 00:00:33.509
procession.

10
00:00:34.209 --> 00:00:38.043
procession means a line of people walking slowly as part of a ceremony.

11
00:00:38.343 --> 00:00:41.364
The wedding procession carried gifts to the bride's house.

12
00:00:42.064 --> 00:00:44.240
Your turn. Say: procession.

13
00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:47.872
procession.

14
00:00:48.883 --> 00:00:50.151
blessing ceremony.

15
00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:54.291
blessing ceremony means a ceremony where monks give good wishes.

16
00:00:54.591 --> 00:00:57.078
We held a blessing ceremony for our new house.

17
00:00:57.778 --> 00:01:00.314
Your turn. Say: blessing ceremony.

18
00:01:03.014 --> 00:01:04.352
blessing ceremony.

19
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:06.061
fortune.

20
00:01:06.761 --> 00:01:09.503
fortune means luck, or what will happen to you in the future.

21
00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:12.790
Some people visit a fortune teller before a big decision.

22
00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.434
Your turn. Say: fortune.

23
00:01:18.134 --> 00:01:18.891
fortune.

24
00:01:19.883 --> 00:01:21.082
pagoda festival.

25
00:01:21.782 --> 00:01:25.314
pagoda festival means a celebration held at a Buddhist temple.

26
00:01:25.614 --> 00:01:28.670
The pagoda festival had music, food and games.

27
00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.778
Your turn. Say: pagoda festival.

28
00:01:34.478 --> 00:01:35.932
pagoda festival.

29
00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:38.150
spirit house.

30
00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:42.974
spirit house means a small shrine where people give offerings to local spirits.

31
00:01:43.274 --> 00:01:46.365
Every morning, Grandma puts flowers in the spirit house.

32
00:01:47.065 --> 00:01:50.042
Your turn. Say: spirit house.

33
00:01:52.742 --> 00:01:53.883
spirit house.

34
00:01:54.883 --> 00:01:55.850
incense.

35
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.594
incense means sticks that make a sweet smell when burned.

36
00:01:59.894 --> 00:02:02.068
The air in the temple smelled of incense.

37
00:02:02.768 --> 00:02:05.002
Your turn. Say: incense.

38
00:02:07.702 --> 00:02:08.843
incense.

39
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:10.886
merit-making.

40
00:02:11.586 --> 00:02:14.387
merit-making means doing good deeds to gain good karma.

41
00:02:14.687 --> 00:02:17.185
Merit-making is an important part of Pchum Ben.

42
00:02:17.885 --> 00:02:20.166
Your turn. Say: merit-making.

43
00:02:22.866 --> 00:02:24.076
merit-making.

44
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:27.094
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:27.394 --> 00:02:30.346
Nita, what's the festival that you enjoy most?

46
00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:35.800
Pchum Ben. It's the festival when we remember our ancestors.

47
00:02:37.117 --> 00:02:38.315
What do people do?

48
00:02:39.617 --> 00:02:43.276
They visit the pagoda which is closest to their home and bring offerings.

49
00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:46.072
Is merit-making important?

50
00:02:47.383 --> 00:02:51.557
Very. The food that we give to monks is for our ancestors' spirits.

51
00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:55.604
Grammar focus: Defining relative clauses.

52
00:02:55.904 --> 00:02:59.425
Defining relative clauses give essential information about a noun.

53
00:02:59.725 --> 00:03:04.371
Use who for people, which or that for things, where for places and when for times.

54
00:03:04.671 --> 00:03:07.994
For example: A monk is a person who lives in a pagoda.

55
00:03:08.294 --> 00:03:12.477
In defining relative clauses, we don't use commas, and that can replace who or which.

56
00:03:13.483 --> 00:03:17.343
Now read and listen. Pchum Ben: The Festival of the Ancestors.

57
00:03:17.643 --> 00:03:22.278
Pchum Ben is a fifteen-day festival which takes place in September or October.

58
00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:27.266
It is the time when Cambodians remember the spirits of their ancestors.

59
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:32.187
Families who live in the city travel home to visit their local pagoda.

60
00:03:33.483 --> 00:03:37.805
They bring offerings of rice and food, and monks lead blessing ceremonies.

61
00:03:39.117 --> 00:03:42.962
Merit-making during Pchum Ben is believed to help ancestors find peace.

62
00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.670
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:49.515
Sticks that smell sweet when burned are blank.

64
00:03:49.815 --> 00:03:53.213
A, incense. B, offerings. C, fortune.

65
00:03:57.217 --> 00:03:59.158
The answer is A: incense.

66
00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.602
A tour guide is a person blank shows tourists around.

67
00:04:03.902 --> 00:04:06.545
A, which. B, who. C, where.

68
00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.143
The answer is B: who.

69
00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.568
This is the village blank I grew up.

70
00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:18.500
A, where. B, which. C, who.

71
00:04:22.517 --> 00:04:24.180
The answer is A: where.

72
00:04:25.683 --> 00:04:28.008
Doing good deeds to gain good karma is blank.

73
00:04:28.308 --> 00:04:32.205
A, procession. B, merit-making. C, spirit house.

74
00:04:36.217 --> 00:04:39.064
The answer is B: merit-making.

75
00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:43.060
According to the text, Pchum Ben lasts blank.

76
00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:47.095
A, three days. B, fifteen days. C, one month.

77
00:04:51.083 --> 00:04:53.559
The answer is B: fifteen days.

78
00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:59.339
Now it's your turn to speak. Describe a festival that is important in your family.

79
00:05:04.639 --> 00:05:11.039
Khmer New Year is the festival when my whole family meets, plays traditional games and visits the pagoda.

80
00:05:11.339 --> 00:05:12.816
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:13.817 --> 00:05:17.978
Great work today! You learned eight new words and defining relative clauses.

82
00:05:18.278 --> 00:05:22.568
Today's value is love of country. Love and take care of Cambodia.

83
00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:25.346
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

84
00:05:25.646 --> 00:05:28.240
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

